  "originalQuery": "A company is evaluating Google Cloud Platform (GCP) database solutions for a new application they are developing. The development team must choose between managed and unmanaged database services. Which of the following statements accurately differentiates between managed and unmanaged database services on GCP?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Managed database services are limited to SQL databases, while unmanaged database services can support NoSQL databases.<br/>B. Managed database services charge for usage based on a pay-as-you-go model, while unmanaged database services have fixed monthly costs.<br/>C. Managed database services provide built-in encryption, while unmanaged database services do not offer any encryption capabilities.<br/>D. Managed database services automatically scale, while unmanaged database services require manual scaling.",
